       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg for extended-release). Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nThe order may have a typo or a unit error. These are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**: 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals**: a typical starting dose, which you can titrate up.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or give me the corrected dose, and I'll enter it right away. I can also add a note to the order, such as \"hold if contrast is given or if eGFR drops.\""
